1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Agents read untrusted email, tickets and screenshots. One hidden instruction can leak a secret. RedLoop is a unit test for that.

2
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:19,400
Same 65 attacks, two agents: our guarded agent, and an unguarded demo agent with no defenses.

3
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:29,000
Thirteen sandboxed scenarios, from email to a screenshot support ticket. An evolutionary attacker keeps the strongest payloads.

4
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:46,500
CI replays all 65 frozen attacks. The build fails, and it shows the ASR.

5
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:58,100
This is the exact payload, and the agent emailing the secret out.

6
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:15,600
Guarded stays green at 0%. And either layer alone still blocks all 65, so one regression doesn't reopen the hole.

7
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:27,300
Live on Muse Spark through the Meta Model API: zero breaches on the frozen suite, about a dollar sixteen per sweep.

8
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:39,000
The live runs also caught a real bug: the agent looped guessing document IDs. A list-docs tool fixed it.

9
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:45,131
RedLoop: find the hole, keep it closed.
